  {
   "id": "s4",
   "type": "drivers",
   "start": 80.692,
   "end": 114.042,
   "audioStart": 80.592,
   "text": "Several key factors shaped performance during the first half of 2026. Regional conflict, production cuts, and shipping disruptions reduced overall sales volumes. Higher selling prices across core segments partly offset these volume declines. Segment results diverged significantly. Petrochemicals posted a net loss due to weaker margins. Conversely, the steel segment grew profit year on year as mothballed capacity successfully restarted. In addition, QVC became a direct holding during the period.",
   "data": {
    "items": [
     "Regional conflict, production cuts and shipping disruptions reduced sales volumes",
     "Selling prices were higher across segments, partly offsetting lower volumes",
     "Petrochemicals segment posted a net loss in H1 2026",
     "Steel segment profit grew year on year; mothballed capacity restarted"
    ],
    "title": "What drove the results"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "s5",
   "type": "segments",
   "start": 115.636,
   "end": 142.823,
   "audioStart": 115.536,
   "text": "Examining the revenue mix during the first half of 2026, operations remained well diversified across core industrial segments. Fertilisers represented the largest share, contributing 38 percent of total revenue. Steel accounted for 36.5 percent of turnover, while petrochemicals generated 25.5 percent. Together, fertilisers and steel provided crucial stability while petrochemical operations faced headwinds.",
   "data": {
    "slices": [
